# Enemy prototype: on the enemy's turn its monster effect goes through the core's chain and the
# player negates it (Infinite Impermanence, which also targets the enemy); its attack uses the
# core's attack declaration and the player gets a response window. The enemy side has no AP;
# the player's AP values are TEST VALUES. Here the enemy is in attack position, where the HP
# rules do not apply (attack-position HP is not decided).
start_draw 0 0
start_draw 1 0
draw_per_turn 1 0
ap 0 5 5
ap_cost 0 set 1
ap_cost 0 activate 1
card 0 mzone 15025844       # Mystical Elf 800/2000, attack position
card 0 hand 10045474        # Infinite Impermanence
card 0 hand 83968380        # Jar of Greed (something to activate at the attack declaration)
card 0 deck 91152256 x10
card 1 mzone 990000001 fu_atk

0 idle sset 10045474
0 idle sset 83968380
0 idle end
expect ap 0 3

1 idle activate 990000001   # Mystical Elf ATK -800
1 select 15025844
0 chain 10045474            # negate the enemy's effects
0 select 990000001
expect chain 10045474 990000001
expect ap 0 2
1 idle battle
1 battle attack 990000001
1 select 15025844
0 chain pass                # the player's response window to the attack declaration
expect lp 0 7600            # 1200 - 800: the ATK drop was negated
expect count 0 mzone 0
expect ap 0 2               # the enemy's attack costs nobody AP
stop
